('127.678.d.5.D',4,'A valid digital signature on a document proves that it:','["was written in English", "came from the signer and was not altered", "is free of viruses", "was printed"]'::jsonb,1,'Signatures verify origin and integrity.','original'),
('127.678.d.5.E',3,'Steganography is the practice of:','["printing a message", "scrambling a message with a key", "hiding a message inside another file such as an image", "deleting a message"]'::jsonb,2,'Steganography conceals data in carriers.','original'),
('127.678.d.5.E',4,'A key difference between steganography and encryption is that steganography hides the:','["length of the key", "file extension", "name of the author", "existence of the message"]'::jsonb,3,'Encryption hides content; steganography hides existence.','original'),
('127.678.d.6.A',3,'A system baseline is a record of:','["normal configuration and performance", "every past error", "the cheapest settings", "only the passwords"]'::jsonb,0,'Baselines capture normal behavior.','original'),
('127.678.d.6.A',4,'Why are baselines useful for security?','["they hide logs", "deviations from normal can reveal compromise", "they make hardware louder", "they replace backups"]'::jsonb,1,'Changes from baseline stand out.','original'),
('127.678.d.6.B',3,'Which is a physical security control?','["a spam filter", "a software patch", "a badge-controlled door", "a password policy"]'::jsonb,2,'Badge readers control physical entry.','original'),
('127.678.d.6.B',4,'Placing servers in a locked room protects them from:','["email phishing", "DNS spoofing", "SQL injection", "unauthorized physical access or theft"]'::jsonb,3,'Locks protect against physical threats.','original'),
('127.678.d.6.C',3,'A device that monitors traffic and alerts on suspicious patterns is an:','["intrusion detection system", "print server", "uninterruptible power supply", "keyboard switch"]'::jsonb,0,'IDS devices monitor and alert.','original'),
('127.678.d.6.C',4,'An intrusion prevention system differs from a detection system because it can:','["only record logs", "actively block malicious traffic", "only play alarms", "only send emails"]'::jsonb,1,'IPS takes action in line with traffic.','original'),
('127.678.d.6.D',3,'Which log pattern is an anomaly worth investigating?','["a nightly backup job", "a routine software check", "logins from two countries within minutes", "a user logging in once each morning"]'::jsonb,2,'Impossible travel suggests compromise.','original'),
('127.678.d.6.D',4,'Reviewing log files for anomalies is easier when the team first knows:','["the monitor brand", "the building floor plan", "the logo color", "what normal activity looks like"]'::jsonb,3,'Normal patterns reveal oddities.','original'),
('127.678.d.6.E',3,'Defense in depth means using:','["multiple layers of security controls", "a single strong firewall only", "no controls", "one password"]'::jsonb,0,'Layers cover for each other.','original'),
('127.678.d.6.E',4,'Which set shows defense in depth?','["one locked door only", "firewall, endpoint protection, access control and training", "one antivirus only", "a single password"]'::jsonb,1,'Several different controls working together.','original'),
('127.678.d.7.A',3,'Network segmentation helps security by:','["sharing one password", "connecting everything together", "limiting how far an attacker can move", "removing firewalls"]'::jsonb,2,'Segments contain breaches.','original'),
('127.678.d.7.A',4,'Placing guest Wi-Fi on a separate segment from internal servers prevents guests from:','["charging phones", "using the internet", "seeing the building", "reaching sensitive internal systems"]'::jsonb,3,'Segmentation separates trust zones.','original'),
('127.678.d.7.B',3,'A VLAN lets administrators:','["group devices logically regardless of physical location", "type faster", "raise screen brightness", "print faster"]'::jsonb,0,'VLANs create logical networks.','original'),
('127.678.d.7.B',4,'Software-defined networking separates the network''s:','["cables from plugs", "control logic from the hardware that forwards traffic", "names from numbers", "screens from keyboards"]'::jsonb,1,'SDN centralizes control in software.','original'),
('127.678.d.7.C',3,'A honeypot is a system designed to:','["store backups", "speed up networks", "attract attackers so their methods can be studied", "print reports"]'::jsonb,2,'Honeypots are decoys.','original'),
('127.678.d.7.C',4,'A honeynet is:','["a type of cable", "a fishing net", "a backup server", "a network of honeypots"]'::jsonb,3,'Honeynets simulate whole networks.','original'),
('127.678.d.7.D',3,'A firewall rule allowing outgoing web traffic on port 443 but blocking all unsolicited incoming connections follows a:','["restrictive policy", "no policy", "open-everything policy", "random policy"]'::jsonb,0,'It allows only what is needed.','original'),
('127.678.d.7.D',4,'A firewall policy that lists exactly which traffic is allowed and blocks everything else is a:','["public policy", "default-deny policy", "disabled policy", "default-allow policy"]'::jsonb,1,'Default deny blocks unlisted traffic.','original'),
('127.678.d.8.A',3,'Several failed logins in a row from one IP address is an indicator of:','["a printer jam", "a software update", "a possible brute-force attack", "a normal reboot"]'::jsonb,2,'Repeated failures suggest password guessing.','original'),
('127.678.d.8.A',4,'A log pattern showing a user account downloading thousands of files in minutes is most consistent with:','["a font install", "routine browsing", "a calendar sync", "data theft"]'::jsonb,3,'Mass downloads are a theft pattern.','original'),
('127.678.d.8.B',3,'Proper data acquisition from a suspect drive uses:','["a verified forensic copy made with a write blocker", "a screenshot of the folder", "a handwritten note", "a quick drag-and-drop copy"]'::jsonb,0,'Forensic copies preserve integrity.','original'),
('127.678.d.8.B',4,'After acquiring a drive image, how can an examiner prove the copy matches the original?','["compare file icons", "compare hash values of both", "compare drive colors", "compare label stickers"]'::jsonb,1,'Matching hashes show identical content.','original'),
('127.678.d.8.C',3,'On a seized laptop, which finding would be suspicious?','["a set of installed fonts", "a folder of family vacation photos", "a hidden folder of stolen customer records", "a browser bookmark list"]'::jsonb,2,'Hidden stolen data is suspicious.','original'),
('127.678.d.8.C',4,'Browser history showing searches on how to wipe logs before an incident is:','["irrelevant to every case", "proof of innocence", "a system backup", "evidence that may show intent"]'::jsonb,3,'Searches can reveal planning.','original'),
('127.678.d.8.D',3,'When critiquing a cybercrime case, an examiner should evaluate:','["how evidence was collected, handled and presented", "the lawyer''s tie", "the courtroom''s color", "the case''s font"]'::jsonb,0,'Evidence handling determines case strength.','original'),
('127.678.d.8.D',4,'A common weakness that can sink a digital evidence case is:','["documented procedures", "a gap in the chain of custody", "a verified image", "too many hash values"]'::jsonb,1,'Gaps cast doubt on evidence.','original'),
('127.678.d.9.A',3,'A managed security service provider (MSSP) offers:','["only printer repair", "only office furniture", "outsourced security monitoring and management", "only paper shredding"]'::jsonb,2,'MSSPs run security services for clients.','original'),
('127.678.d.9.A',4,'A small business with no security staff might choose Security as a Service to:','["avoid all risk permanently", "stop using computers", "remove all employees", "get expert monitoring without hiring a full team"]'::jsonb,3,'Outsourcing gives access to expertise.','original'),
('127.678.d.9.B',3,'Machine learning helps security tools by:','["spotting unusual patterns in large amounts of data", "replacing all analysts overnight", "preventing every attack", "making passwords unnecessary"]'::jsonb,0,'ML finds anomalies at scale.','original'),
('127.678.d.9.B',4,'A risk of relying only on AI-based detection is that attackers may:','["turn off electricity", "craft inputs to evade or fool the model", "delete the model''s name", "remove the internet"]'::jsonb,1,'Adversarial inputs can evade models.','original'),
('127.678.d.9.C',3,'Predictive analytics in cybersecurity uses past data to:','["repair hardware", "change history", "forecast likely future threats", "erase old logs"]'::jsonb,2,'Patterns in history suggest future risks.','original'),
('127.678.d.9.C',4,'A benefit of predictive analytics for defenders is the ability to:','["avoid training", "ignore warnings", "skip patching", "prepare for attacks before they occur"]'::jsonb,3,'Forecasts enable proactive defense.','original'),
('127.678.d.9.D',3,'Quantum computers could threaten current public key encryption because they may be able to:','["solve certain math problems much faster", "store only text", "connect without power", "print faster"]'::jsonb,0,'Quantum algorithms threaten some cryptography.','original'),
('127.678.d.9.D',4,'Researchers developing encryption designed to resist quantum computers are working on:','["pre-digital cryptography", "post-quantum cryptography", "analog cryptography", "paper cryptography"]'::jsonb,1,'Post-quantum algorithms resist quantum attacks.','original'),
('127.678.d.10.A',3,'In a Linux terminal, which command lists the files in a directory?','["rm", "mv", "ls", "cd"]'::jsonb,2,'ls lists directory contents.','original'),
('127.678.d.10.A',4,'Which command changes the current directory?','["cp", "mkdir", "ls", "cd"]'::jsonb,3,'cd means change directory.','original'),
('127.678.d.10.B',3,'In Linux, the top of the file system hierarchy is the:','["root directory (/)", "C: drive", "downloads folder", "desktop folder"]'::jsonb,0,'Everything sits under the root.','original'),
('127.678.d.10.B',4,'Windows typically labels storage volumes with:','["numbers in parentheses", "drive letters such as C:", "emoji", "only slashes"]'::jsonb,1,'Windows uses drive letters.','original'),
('127.678.d.10.C',3,'Which Linux command copies a file?','["rm", "pwd", "cp", "ls"]'::jsonb,2,'cp copies files.','original'),
('127.678.d.10.C',4,'Which command displays the contents of a text file on screen?','["mkdir", "cd", "touch", "cat"]'::jsonb,3,'cat prints file contents.','original'),
('127.678.d.10.D',3,'The ping command is used to test:','["whether a host is reachable on the network", "a file''s size", "a monitor''s refresh rate", "a printer''s ink"]'::jsonb,0,'Ping checks reachability.','original'),
('127.678.d.10.D',4,'On Windows, which command-line tool lists a computer''s network adapter addresses and settings?','["ifconfig", "ipconfig", "pwd", "ls"]'::jsonb,1,'ipconfig shows Windows network settings.','original'),
('127.678.d.11.A',3,'When a team writes a technical report together, one good practice is to:','["skip reviews", "let everyone use different styles", "assign sections and agree on a common format", "write without outlines"]'::jsonb,2,'Shared structure keeps reports consistent.','original'),
('127.678.d.11.A',4,'Using a shared document with version history helps a team:','["prevent collaboration", "limit comments", "hide changes", "track edits and avoid overwriting each other''s work"]'::jsonb,3,'Version history protects contributions.','original'),
('127.678.d.11.B',3,'A summary of technical findings should include:','["key results, evidence and recommendations", "blank sections", "unrelated stories", "only opinions"]'::jsonb,0,'Findings need support and next steps.','original'),
('127.678.d.11.B',4,'Peer review of a technical report is valuable because reviewers can:','["hide the findings", "catch errors and unclear explanations", "remove all evidence", "add unrelated content"]'::jsonb,1,'Fresh eyes improve quality.','original'),
('127.678.d.11.C',3,'To explain a firewall to a non-technical audience, a presenter could compare it to:','["a complicated code listing", "a packet dump", "a security guard checking who enters a building", "a blank slide"]'::jsonb,2,'Analogies make concepts accessible.','original'),
('127.678.d.11.C',4,'When presenting findings to executives, it is most important to:','["read every log line", "use maximum jargon", "avoid conclusions", "focus on business impact and recommended actions"]'::jsonb,3,'Leaders need impact and decisions.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.A',3,'Replacing a device''s chip with a tampered component is an attack on:','["hardware", "software", "network traffic", "a database query"]'::jsonb,0,'Tampering with parts is a hardware attack.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.A',4,'Flooding a network with traffic to cause an outage is primarily a:','["hardware attack", "network attack", "print job", "firmware update"]'::jsonb,1,'Traffic floods target network availability.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.B',3,'A blended threat combines:','["only physical theft", "a single simple virus", "multiple attack methods, such as malware and social engineering", "one password guess"]'::jsonb,2,'Blended threats mix techniques.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.B',4,'Why are blended threats difficult to defend against?','["they use only one method", "they are always visible", "they require no tools", "they exploit several weaknesses at once"]'::jsonb,3,'Multiple vectors strain defenses.','original')
