       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_83_v1'
from (values
('127.678.d.12.C',3,'Losing customers after a data breach is mainly a:','["business risk", "printing risk", "weather risk", "hardware risk"]'::jsonb,0,'Reputation harms the business.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.C',4,'The cost of fines and legal fees after a breach is a:','["physical risk", "financial risk", "musical risk", "visual risk"]'::jsonb,1,'Breaches create monetary losses.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.D',3,'Installing a firewall and patching systems to lower the chance or impact of an attack is risk:','["avoidance", "transference", "mitigation", "acceptance"]'::jsonb,2,'Mitigation reduces likelihood or impact.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.D',4,'A company knowingly keeps a very low-impact risk because fixing it costs more than the harm. This is risk:','["mitigation", "transference", "avoidance", "acceptance"]'::jsonb,3,'Acceptance tolerates the risk.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.E',3,'After a scan finds weak passwords, a preventative measure is to:','["enforce a stronger password policy", "disable logging", "remove all accounts", "share the weak passwords"]'::jsonb,0,'Policy fixes the found weakness.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.E',4,'A prevention plan should assign each fix an owner and a:','["mascot", "deadline", "slogan", "wallpaper"]'::jsonb,1,'Owners and deadlines ensure follow-through.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.F',3,'The CVE list is a public catalog of:','["popular passwords", "software prices", "known security vulnerabilities", "hardware warranties"]'::jsonb,2,'CVE identifies known vulnerabilities.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.F',4,'Which database, run by NIST, lists vulnerability details and severity scores?','["the National Weather Service", "the Social Security database", "the Library of Congress catalog", "the National Vulnerability Database (NVD)"]'::jsonb,3,'NVD adds scoring to CVE entries.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.G',3,'A web form that lets attackers run database commands is vulnerable to:','["SQL injection", "cookie baking", "screen scraping", "pixel injection"]'::jsonb,0,'Unsanitized input reaches the database.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.G',4,'A site that returns user-supplied text without sanitizing it can allow:','["screen burn-in", "cross-site scripting", "disk fragmentation", "fan failure"]'::jsonb,1,'Unsanitized output enables XSS.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.H',3,'Overwriting a drive with random data so the original data cannot be recovered is called:','["indexing", "defragmenting", "wiping", "mirroring"]'::jsonb,2,'Wiping overwrites old data.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.H',4,'Using a strong magnetic field to erase data on magnetic media is:','["compiling", "streaming", "pinging", "degaussing"]'::jsonb,3,'Degaussing scrambles magnetic data.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.I',3,'In a ransomware scenario, an early containment step is to:','["isolate affected systems from the network", "pay immediately", "email the attacker", "reboot everything"]'::jsonb,0,'Isolation stops the spread.','original'),
('127.678.d.12.I',4,'A scenario-based response plan should name:','["the building color", "who does what at each stage", "the CEO''s pets", "a menu of snacks"]'::jsonb,1,'Clear roles speed response.','original'),
('127.678.d.13.A',3,'The Zero Trust model assumes:','["firewalls make checks unnecessary", "passwords are enough", "no user or device is trusted by default", "everyone inside the network is trusted"]'::jsonb,2,'Zero Trust verifies everything.','original'),
('127.678.d.13.A',4,'A core idea of Zero Trust is to:','["remove authentication", "trust all internal traffic", "share admin credentials", "verify every access request continuously"]'::jsonb,3,'Continuous verification is central.','original'),
('127.678.d.13.B',3,'A multi-factor plan for admin logins could require:','["a password plus a hardware security key", "a longer username", "the same password twice", "two usernames"]'::jsonb,0,'Two different factor types.','original'),
('127.678.d.13.B',4,'Adding a second factor mainly defends against:','["broken monitors", "stolen or guessed passwords", "slow typing", "low battery"]'::jsonb,1,'A password alone is not enough.','original'),
('127.678.d.13.C',3,'A disaster recovery plan describes how to:','["buy furniture", "hire interns", "restore systems and data after a major disruption", "avoid backups"]'::jsonb,2,'DRPs guide restoration.','original'),
('127.678.d.13.C',4,'Two key goals in a DRP are the recovery time objective and the:','["reporting period objective", "recruiting plan objective", "resource purchasing objective", "recovery point objective"]'::jsonb,3,'RTO and RPO set time and data-loss limits.','original'),
('127.678.d.14.A',3,'A fence, a lock and a security guard are examples of:','["physical security controls", "software patches", "encryption keys", "network protocols"]'::jsonb,0,'They protect physical access.','original'),
('127.678.d.14.A',4,'A mantrap (two interlocking doors) is used to prevent:','["power surges", "tailgating into secure areas", "email spam", "disk errors"]'::jsonb,1,'Mantraps admit one person at a time.','original'),
('127.678.d.14.B',3,'Heating, ventilation and air conditioning (HVAC) systems matter to data centers because they:','["encrypt files", "install updates", "keep equipment within safe temperatures", "print documents"]'::jsonb,2,'Overheating damages hardware.','original'),
('127.678.d.14.B',4,'A data center''s automatic fire suppression system is an example of an:','["email filter", "password manager", "browser plug-in", "embedded system protecting physical assets"]'::jsonb,3,'Embedded controls protect facilities.','original'),
('127.679.d.1.A',3,'A help desk technician''s daily duties usually include:','["troubleshooting user computer problems", "driving buses", "cooking meals", "designing buildings"]'::jsonb,0,'Help desk staff solve user issues.','original'),
('127.679.d.1.A',4,'Which entry-level IT job focuses on installing and repairing computers and peripherals?','["software architect", "computer support technician", "systems auditor", "chief technology officer"]'::jsonb,1,'Support technicians install and repair equipment.','original'),
('127.679.d.1.B',3,'CompTIA A+ is an entry-level certification that validates skills in:','["cooking", "accounting", "computer hardware and troubleshooting", "nursing"]'::jsonb,2,'A+ covers hardware and support skills.','original'),
('127.679.d.1.B',4,'On an IT resume, listing certifications and hands-on lab experience shows:','["only classroom attendance", "unrelated interests", "a lack of training", "verified skills and practical ability"]'::jsonb,3,'Credentials and labs prove ability.','original'),
('127.679.d.2.A',3,'When a customer describes a computer problem in non-technical terms, a technician should:','["listen carefully and ask clear follow-up questions", "interrupt often", "dismiss the problem", "use confusing jargon"]'::jsonb,0,'Good communication gathers accurate details.','original'),
('127.679.d.2.A',4,'A written service ticket should include:','["only the technician''s lunch plans", "the problem description, steps taken and the result", "nothing", "a joke"]'::jsonb,1,'Tickets document work for future reference.','original'),
('127.679.d.2.B',3,'A wiring diagram or schematic helps a technician:','["choose a desktop theme", "find a lunch spot", "see how components are connected", "pick a font"]'::jsonb,2,'Diagrams show connections.','original'),
('127.679.d.2.B',4,'Before replacing a part, a technician should consult the device''s:','["decorative poster", "gift card", "calendar", "service manual or technical documentation"]'::jsonb,3,'Manuals give correct procedures.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.A',3,'The central processing unit (CPU) is a microprocessor that:','["executes program instructions", "displays images only", "stores files permanently", "prints documents"]'::jsonb,0,'The CPU runs instructions.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.A',4,'The CPU''s basic cycle of operation is:','["type, click, drag", "fetch, decode, execute", "save, close, open", "print, scan, copy"]'::jsonb,1,'Fetch-decode-execute is the instruction cycle.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.B',3,'In binary logic, an AND gate outputs 1 only when:','["the inputs differ", "either input is 1", "both inputs are 1", "both inputs are 0"]'::jsonb,2,'AND needs both inputs true.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.B',4,'The binary number 1001 equals what in decimal?','["5", "13", "11", "9"]'::jsonb,3,'8 + 1 = 9.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.C',3,'Which unit measures electrical current?','["ampere", "watt", "volt", "ohm"]'::jsonb,0,'Current is measured in amperes.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.C',4,'Using Ohm''s law, a circuit with 12 volts and 4 ohms of resistance has a current of:','["0.33 amperes", "3 amperes", "8 amperes", "48 amperes"]'::jsonb,1,'Current equals voltage divided by resistance.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.D',3,'A common first step in troubleshooting a computer that will not turn on is to:','["reinstall the OS", "replace the CPU", "check the power cable and outlet", "buy a new monitor"]'::jsonb,2,'Check the simplest causes first.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.D',4,'Which troubleshooting practice is best?','["assume the cause", "skip documentation", "change many things at once", "change one thing at a time and test the result"]'::jsonb,3,'One change at a time isolates the cause.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.E',3,'A signal that varies continuously, like a sound wave, is:','["analog", "binary", "discrete", "digital"]'::jsonb,0,'Analog signals are continuous.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.E',4,'Digital signals represent information using:','["temperatures only", "discrete values such as 0 and 1", "colors only", "continuous waves only"]'::jsonb,1,'Digital data uses distinct levels.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.F',3,'Bandwidth is the:','["price of a router", "color of a connector", "amount of data that can be transmitted in a given time", "length of a cable"]'::jsonb,2,'Bandwidth measures capacity.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.F',4,'In data communication, a protocol is a:','["power supply rating", "kind of monitor", "type of cable", "set of rules for exchanging data"]'::jsonb,3,'Protocols define how devices communicate.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.G',3,'A computer system''s architecture describes:','["how its hardware components are organized and connect", "its warranty length", "its color", "its price"]'::jsonb,0,'Architecture is the system''s organization.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.G',4,'A server differs from a typical desktop in that it is designed to:','["only print labels", "provide services to many other computers", "only browse the web", "only play games"]'::jsonb,1,'Servers serve clients.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.H',3,'The main circuit board that connects the CPU, memory and other components is the:','["power cord", "heat sink", "motherboard", "speaker"]'::jsonb,2,'The motherboard links the components.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.H',4,'The power supply unit (PSU) in a desktop:','["stores programs", "displays video", "cools the case", "converts AC wall power into DC power for components"]'::jsonb,3,'PSUs convert and distribute power.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.I',3,'A device that protects computers from sudden power spikes is a:','["surge protector", "speaker", "mouse pad", "webcam"]'::jsonb,0,'Surge protectors absorb voltage spikes.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.I',4,'An uninterruptible power supply (UPS) mainly provides:','["faster internet", "battery power during outages", "extra storage", "wireless signals"]'::jsonb,1,'UPS units keep systems running briefly.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.J',3,'Which is an emerging technology that may affect computer technicians?','["dot-matrix ribbons", "typewriters", "artificial intelligence and internet-connected smart devices", "floppy disks"]'::jsonb,2,'New technology changes the field.','original'),
('127.679.d.3.J',4,'Technicians keep current with new technology mainly by:','["using only old manuals", "avoiding all change", "ignoring new tools", "ongoing training and reading industry updates"]'::jsonb,3,'Continuous learning keeps skills current.','original'),
('127.679.d.4.A',3,'The component that temporarily holds data the CPU is actively using is:','["random access memory (RAM)", "the hard drive", "the keyboard", "the monitor"]'::jsonb,0,'RAM provides fast working storage.','original'),
('127.679.d.4.A',4,'Permanent long-term storage of files is the job of the:','["CPU cache", "storage drive", "RAM", "video card"]'::jsonb,1,'Drives keep data when powered off.','original'),
('127.679.d.4.B',3,'Smartphones connect to cellular networks using:','["a serial printer", "a parallel cable", "a radio transceiver and a SIM or eSIM", "a power strip"]'::jsonb,2,'Cellular radios and SIMs identify the device.','original')
