('127.679.d.4.E',4,'To interpret a beep code, a technician should consult the:','["weather report", "motherboard or BIOS manufacturer''s documentation", "phone book", "printer manual"]'::jsonb,1,'Codes differ by manufacturer.','original'),
('127.679.d.4.F',3,'An interrupt is a signal that:','["turns off the CPU", "deletes memory", "tells the CPU a device needs attention", "prints a page"]'::jsonb,2,'Interrupts request CPU service.','original'),
('127.679.d.4.F',4,'Giving a high-priority device, like a keyboard press, immediate attention from the CPU relies on:','["screen resolution", "file names", "fonts", "interrupt priorities"]'::jsonb,3,'Priorities decide which interrupt goes first.','original'),
