('127.679.d.6.A',3,'A graphical user interface (GUI) lets users interact using:','["Morse code", "command lines only", "windows, icons and menus", "punch cards"]'::jsonb,2,'GUIs are visual.','original'),
('127.679.d.6.A',4,'A toolbar in an application is a row of:','["storage chips", "power cables", "fans", "buttons for common commands"]'::jsonb,3,'Toolbars give quick access to functions.','original'),
('127.679.d.6.B',3,'When choosing between two spreadsheet programs, a technician should compare:','["features, compatibility and cost", "slogan", "logo shape", "box color"]'::jsonb,0,'Practical criteria drive the choice.','original'),
('127.679.d.6.B',4,'Before recommending software to a department, it is wise to:','["skip testing", "test it against the department''s needs", "pick at random", "buy the most expensive"]'::jsonb,1,'Testing confirms fit.','original'),
('127.679.d.6.C',3,'Before installing software, a technician should verify that:','["it is downloaded from anywhere", "it is the newest version", "the organization has a valid license for it", "it has a nice icon"]'::jsonb,2,'Licensing must be confirmed.','original'),
('127.679.d.6.C',4,'Installing a pirated copy of commercial software can expose an organization to:','["lower costs only", "better support", "automatic updates", "legal penalties and malware"]'::jsonb,3,'Piracy brings legal and security risks.','original'),
('127.679.d.6.D',3,'Software delivered over the internet by subscription is known as:','["Software as a Service (SaaS)", "firmware", "shareware cartridge", "freeware drivers"]'::jsonb,0,'SaaS is subscription software online.','original'),
('127.679.d.6.D',4,'A site license allows software to be used:','["only once", "by many users at one organization", "by one person only", "by no one"]'::jsonb,1,'Site licenses cover an organization.','original'),
('127.679.d.6.E',3,'If an application freezes, a reasonable first step is to:','["replace the motherboard", "buy a new computer", "close and restart it, then check for updates", "delete the operating system"]'::jsonb,2,'Start with simple fixes.','original'),
('127.679.d.6.E',4,'After a recent update, a program crashes. Which action may help identify the cause?','["reformat the drive immediately", "ignore the crash", "unplug the monitor", "check error logs and consider rolling back the update"]'::jsonb,3,'Logs and rollbacks isolate update problems.','original'),
('127.679.d.7.A',3,'The hardware part that lets a desktop computer physically join a wired or wireless network is the NIC. It allows the computer to:','["connect to a network", "print documents", "store backups", "play audio"]'::jsonb,0,'A NIC is the network connection hardware.','original'),
('127.679.d.7.A',4,'Which connector is most often used for wired Ethernet?','["3.5 mm audio", "RJ-45", "VGA", "HDMI"]'::jsonb,1,'Ethernet cables use RJ-45.','original'),
('127.679.d.7.B',3,'After connecting a computer to a network, it typically receives an IP address from a:','["mail server", "print server", "DHCP server", "game server"]'::jsonb,2,'DHCP assigns addresses automatically.','original'),
('127.679.d.7.B',4,'To join a Wi-Fi network, a user generally needs the network''s name and its:','["monitor size", "serial number", "room number", "security key or password"]'::jsonb,3,'The key authenticates the user.','original'),
('127.679.d.7.C',3,'A computer cannot reach any website. Which should a technician check first?','["whether the cable or Wi-Fi connection is active", "the keyboard layout", "the printer ink", "the desktop wallpaper"]'::jsonb,0,'Check the physical or wireless link first.','original'),
('127.679.d.7.C',4,'If pinging the default gateway fails, the problem is most likely in the:','["remote website''s content", "local connection or network configuration", "monitor settings", "user''s resume"]'::jsonb,1,'The gateway is the first hop out.','original')
